//! Expression evaluation engine.
//!
//! This was `eval_y.c`, generated by bison from `eval.y`. The LALR tables and
//! the `yyparse` driver are gone — the front end is now hand-written safe Rust
//! in `crate::parser` (see `PARSER_SPEC.md` and `PARSER_MIGRATION.md`). What
//! remains is the part bison never generated: the `New_*` builders that
//! assemble the `Node` arena, and the `Do_*` routines that evaluate it a
//! row-chunk at a time.
//!
//! The grammar rules, rather than evaluating an expression in situ, build a
//! tree mapping out the order of operations and dependencies. This
//! "compilation" allows much faster processing of multiple rows; the technique
//! was developed by Uwe Lammers of the XMM Science Analysis System, although
//! the CFITSIO implementation is entirely original code.

